{
  "case_id": "2020-19-199",
  "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HARRIS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Because Congress, in Section 355(f), subjected any final decision of the Railroad Retirement Board to judicial review, all final decisions, including reopening denials, are reviewable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 19-199, Salinas versus United States Railroad Retirement Board. Ms. Harris."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Ms. Harris, what is the statutory or regulatory basis for the reopening? Do you -- and what I'm getting at is whether or not you have a stated right to a reopening."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, my question was basically the same as the Chief Justice's, and it seems to me on that question you have going against you, first, the language of it, of rights and liabilities, read in light of what we said in two cases. It's both Your Home Visiting Nurse and also Califano v. Sanders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I'm interested in the interplay between the Railroad Retirement Act and the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act. This is a case under the former. Is there any reason why we can't decide it simply by looking at the language of that provision, Section 231g?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Ms. Harris, could I ask you a little bit more about this distinction you're making between new evidence claims and rehashed claims? And this really goes back to Justice Breyer's question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Okay. Can I ask you a question about 355, go back to where you started? I guess I don't quite understand your argument there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Good morning, Ms. Harris. Let me pick up right there. Let -- let -- let's suppose for the purposes of this question that I agree with you that under 355(f), reopening petitions could be reviewed under the RUIA. But let's also suppose that the language in 231g suggests that reopening petitions under the RRA cannot."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HARRIS: Well, a couple of points on that. First of all, with respect to the text of 355(g), that is a review exclusivity provision under the RUIA, and it says -- it is talking about the determination of any claim for benefits or refunds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF AUSTIN RAYNOR ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Maybe. But why isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, I'm not sure I understand the answer. Is -- is the answer that you really think that it would be a mistake -- it would be -- it would be wrong as a matter of law or it would create anomalies if we were to decide the case based solely on 231g?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "990193c52e02034416020633723d2ee2612a185b13b567f909aff449d36a0991",
      "evidence_id": "ev-990193c52e02-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner argued below that there was an error on the face of the record. That was his basis for reopening in the Fifth Circuit."
    },
    {
